Control objective:
Per paragraph 67 of Prudential Standard APS 113 Capital Adequacy, the objective of the control is to ensure that independent review and approval of the Business Division Credit Risk Rating System (CRRS) is performed in a timely manner, annually. This is a non-key control pertaining to the divisional review of the CRRS. Refer to CTL004652 which is a key control that rolls-up divisional CRRS reviews for independent review and approval of the Group Credit Risk Rating System by the GCCO. Requirements, roles and responsibilities for the CRRS review are documented in section 01.09 Credit Risk Rating System in BB & WIB Credit Policies on the Intranet.

Detailed description:
Paragraph 67 of Prudential Standard APS 113 Capital Adequacy: Internal Ratings-based Approach to Credit Risk states: An ADI’s rating system and its operations, including the operations of the credit risk control function and the estimation of PD and, where relevant, LGD and EAD, must be reviewed at least annually by an independent function. This review must include adherence to all applicable minimum requirements detailed in this Attachment. The findings of this review must be documented. To meet the requirements of this standard, on an annual basis, Business Lending Risk Portfolio Management undertakes a review of the Business Division Credit Risk Rating System, which is for approval by the Group Chief Credit Officer (or delegate). Data analysis / commentary summarised in the report includes key factors underpinning Customer Risk Grade (CRG) and Loss Given Default (LGD) accuracy and therefore supporting (or otherwise) the efficacy thereof, viz: model outcomes versus overrides (includes findings of annual model reviews approved by the Credit Risk Estimates Committee (CREC)), annual CRG / LGD refresh processes, tracking and completion of annual / interim reviews, plus other policies which support CRG / LGD assignment, matured facilities, volume and mix of policy exceptions, timeliness of policy reviews (where required), credit data integrity testing and Credit Risk Review testing outcomes. On completion, a draft 'Memorandum to Group Chief Credit Officer' (the Memo) is circulated for review / discussion, with feedback incorporated as required; final version of the Memo (and recommendation(s) therein), is supported by the Head of Risk Business Lending and the Head of Credit Optimisation (BL LOB), and submitted to Group Chief Credit Officer (or delegate) for review and approval. The annual rating system review process is initiated at the request of Senior Manager, Credit Risk Policy, Credit Risk, who manages the annual Credit Risk Rating System review process on behalf of GCCO. Senior Manager, Credit Risk Policy, Credit Risk follows up to ensure that requisite paper(s) is/are received by the due date, and in an acceptable format. Business Division Credit Risk Rating System Review Report is produced by Business Lending Risk Portfolio Management. Head of Risk Business Lending and the Head of Credit Optimisation (BL LOB) review and support to GCCO (or delegate) for approval.

How evidenced:
Compliance is evidenced by completion of the Annual risk rating review with approval from Group Chief Credit Officer (or delegate)(electronic) of the Memo.

How monitored:
Senior Manager, Credit Risk Policy, Credit Risk follows up to ensure that requisite paper(s) is/are received by the due date, and in an acceptable format.

